        "--title",
        "comparison launch",
        "svgo's removeScripts plugin (plugins/removeScripts.js) removes scripting from an SVG: script elements, event attributes, executable attributes of HTML inside foreignObject, and links with an executable URL. A link is an <a> element whose href or *:href attribute is a javascript: or vbscript: URL, or a data: URL of an HTML, XHTML or SVG document; the plugin replaces such an element by its element children (its text children are dropped). Whether a URL is executable is decided by isExecutableUrl in lib/svgo/tools.js, which hasScripts in the same file also uses, so other plugins (cleanupIds, minifyStyles, removeHiddenElems, removeUselessStrokeAndFill) leave documents with executable links alone. Two kinds of executable link survive today. First, an SVG anchor written with a namespace prefix: in <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:svg=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><svg:a xlink:href=\"javascript:alert(1)\"><rect width=\"1\"/></svg:a></svg> the svg:a element is kept with its link, although it is an SVG <a>. Second, a URL whose scheme is split by ASCII tab, line feed or carriage return characters, such as href=\"java&#9;script:alert(1)\": browsers remove those characters from a URL before parsing it, so the link runs, but isExecutableUrl does not recognise it. Fix both. An element is an SVG anchor when its local name is a and it is unprefixed (as today) or its prefix resolves to the SVG namespace http://www.w3.org/2000/svg through the xmlns: declarations in scope at that element, counting declarations on the element itself and, where a prefix is redeclared on a descendant, the innermost one; an a element whose prefix resolves to another namespace is not an anchor and keeps its attributes and children. isExecutableUrl must ignore ASCII tab (U+0009), line feed (U+000A) and carriage return (U+000D) anywhere in the value, so that every user of it (removeScripts for links and for URL attributes of HTML inside foreignObject, and hasScripts) treats such a URL as executable: for example isExecutableUrl('java\\tscript:alert(1)') and isExecutableUrl('data:text/ht\\nml,x') must be true. What must not change: unprefixed anchors are handled as today; links with non-executable URLs (https: and relative URLs, #fragments, data:image/png and other inert data URLs, a scheme broken by a space) are kept; an anchor whose prefix resolves to another namespace is kept; script elements (prefixed or not, in the SVG or XHTML namespace), event attributes, and srcdoc, on* and executable URL attributes of HTML inside foreignObject are removed as today; and the output of every plugin, preset-default included, is unchanged for documents without such links. The plugin tests are fixture files test/plugins/<plugin>.<n>.svg.txt (a description, ===, the input, @@@, the expected output), run by test/plugins/_index.test.js. Add regression tests for this behaviour to the project's existing test suite. The project's tests run with npm test (vitest run, which also type-checks the JavaScript under tsconfig.json's strict checkJs).\n\nVisible acceptance check (it must pass; it is not the only criterion): node acceptance/visible/check.mjs\nThe project's own tests run with: npm test\nDeliverables, all required; the task is not done until each is in the tree:\n1. The implementation of the behaviour described above, in the project's own source.\n2. Regression tests: at least one new test case, in the project's own test directory and style, that fails on the current code and passes with your change, adding at least one new assertion. A change without a new test is incomplete.\n3. The visible acceptance check (node acceptance/visible/check.mjs) and the project's own test command (npm test) both passing on the final tree.\nAllowed changes: implementation code, and regression tests for the change (new test files, or new cases added to existing test files, in the project's own test directory and style).\nDo not modify anything under acceptance/visible/.\nDo not change how the project's checks run: leave the test and coverage configuration files (.taprc*, .nycrc*, .c8rc*, .mocharc*, jest.config.*, vitest.config.*, ava.config.*, karma.conf.*) and the test, pretest and posttest scripts and runner sections of package.json as they are.\nDo not delete or weaken existing tests: keep every existing assertion (it may move to another test file), add no skip, only or todo markers, and add no coverage-ignore pragmas. A change that does any of these is rejected at evaluation whatever else passes."
      ],
